<title>USA: Echo Bay Mines says Kraus resigns as CEO.</title>
<headline>Echo Bay Mines says Kraus resigns as CEO.</headline>
<dateline>ENGLEWOOD, Colo. 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Echo Bay Mines Ltd said on Tuesday that its president, director and chief executive officer Richard Kraus had resigned.</p>
<p>The company said his responsibilities would be assumed on an interim basis by Robert Leclerc, who has served the company as chairman since May 1996 and as director since 1992.</p>
<p>Echo Bay is a gold producer with mines in Canada and the United States and with exploration and development projects on four continents.</p>
</text>
